Also the car number decals: `decal.rotation.x = -Math.PI/2` only; plane faces up. Fine.

Now, grandstand crowd: mesh boxes with the crowd texture; UVs per face repeated 1x → the 256×128 texture stretched over a 26×0.82 face → giant dots. Hmm, BoxGeometry UVs map the full texture to each face. With a 26m wide face and a 256px texture, dots would be 0.2m wide — actually reasonable (people 0.5m wide, our dots are 2.4px of 256 → 0.24m at 26m). Dots too small? People would be ~0.5m → 5px. Our dots 2.4-4px → 0.24-0.4m. Fine! The x repetition is 1 per face, so 256 dots across 26m → each dot ~0.25m. Reasonable.

The crowd texture is on all box faces including the top; acceptable.

Now lighting may still be off. Let's test.

But also fix: the `applyWeather` early-return on `this.weather === w`; on load `this.weather=null`, fine. However after `unload`, `this.weather` remains the old value; `load` sets `this.weather=null` before applyWeather. Yes.

Test again: reload, quick race, wait. The headless FPS is ~5 so countdown slow; that's fine. Screenshot at start after load.

